[{:adr/authoritative_for ["aiueos owns Layer 1 (capability decision authority: manifest validation, policy reasoning, grant/deny decisions via aiueos.broker/verify-one|verify-system, audit trail, signing/trust) and NEVER owns execution -- permanently, by design, not a gap. aiueos.broker's own docstring states this explicitly; a future change proposing a Chicory/wasmtime/etc dependency in aiueos contradicts this ADR and needs an explicit new one to override it, not accretion" "kototama owns Layer 3 (the Wasm execution runtime -- kototama.tender JVM/Chicory + actor-host.js browser-native, both implementing kototama.contract's actor:host ABI) and NEVER decides a grant itself -- every HostCaps it enforces is either caller-supplied or derived via the one sanctioned boundary below" "kototama.aiueos-adapter (kotoba-lang/kototama, ADR-2607062330 addendum 7 / kototama#24) is the ONLY sanctioned integration point -- calls aiueos.cli/command-result and translates the real decision into a kototama.contract/host-caps value, no re-derivation, no second decision-making anywhere else in either repo" "aiueos.decide (nbb-decide subprocess, newline-delimited EDN) and aiueos.cli/command-result (in-process) are the same Layer 1 decision exposed two ways for two caller shapes (non-JVM host vs already-JVM host) -- not two different decisions" "coverage of the adapter (log-write/clock-monotonic/random-bytes, aiueos's default kernel capabilities) is intentionally partial -- gen-keypair/sign/verify/sha256-hex/http-post/log-read have no aiueos-kernel-capability counterpart and stay caller-supplied HostCaps on purpose, since widening aiueos's kernel-capability vocabulary to cover kototama's own crypto/identity surface would itself be a boundary violation in the other direction" "consolidates and supersedes-in-spirit (not in force -- no prior ADR is retracted) the scattered decision trail across ADR-2607022200/2607022700/2607022900/2607062330(+addenda 1,6,7)/2607062400, written specifically because that trail includes TWO separate false claims (ADR-2607022900, ADR-2607062330's original addendum) that a specific aiueos execution implementation already existed -- both verified false later in the same ADR history"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "aiueos-kototama-decision-execution-boundary", :adr/related ["adr-2607022200" "adr-2607022700" "adr-2607022900" "adr-2607062330" "adr-2607062400" "adr-2607061630" "adr-2607030900"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607072400-aiueos-kototama-decision-execution-boundary", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-07", :adr/body "see 2607072400-aiueos-kototama-decision-execution-boundary.edn", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/artifacts "{:aiueos \"kotoba-lang/aiueos (Layer 1 -- aiueos.decide/aiueos.cli/aiueos.broker/aiueos.policy, no changes made by this ADR) — 139 tests/399 assertions green\", :kototama \"kotoba-lang/kototama (Layer 3 -- kototama.tender + kototama.aiueos-adapter, no changes made by this ADR) — 25 tests/50 assertions green\"}", :adr/date "2026-07-07", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607072400: aiueos ⊣ kototama — the decision/execution boundary, stated once", :adr/source-format "edn"}]